{"schemaVersion":1,"generatedAt":"2026-08-16T16:20:46.501Z","id":"73e36eabbfaa35053d6de45d","canonicalUrl":"https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260815005915.1097270-1-i.maximets%40ovn.org/","channels":["lkml"],"thread":{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"thread:lore-git:20260815005915.1097270-1-i.maximets@ovn.org","source":{"kind":"static-generated","canonicalThreadUrl":"https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260815005915.1097270-1-i.maximets%40ovn.org/","fetchedAt":"2026-08-16T16:20:46.501Z","contentDigest":"lore-git:20260815005915.1097270-1-i.maximets@ovn.org"},"subject":"Re: [PATCH net] net: openvswitch: fix flow mask use-after-free on flow deletion","messages":{"f7t5x1anmmm.fsf@aconole-thinkpadt14gen4.rmtusnh.csb":{"id":"f7t5x1anmmm.fsf@aconole-thinkpadt14gen4.rmtusnh.csb","messageId":"f7t5x1anmmm.fsf@aconole-thinkpadt14gen4.rmtusnh.csb","references":["20260815005915.1097270-1-i.maximets@ovn.org"],"missingAncestorIds":["20260815005915.1097270-1-i.maximets@ovn.org"],"author":{"name":"Aaron Conole","address":"aconole@redhat.com"},"replyTo":[],"to":[{"name":"Ilya Maximets","address":"i.maximets@ovn.org"}],"cc":[{"name":"","address":"netdev@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"Eelco Chaudron","address":"echaudro@redhat.com"},{"name":"David S. Miller","address":"davem@davemloft.net"},{"name":"Eric Dumazet","address":"edumazet@google.com"},{"name":"Jakub Kicinski","address":"kuba@kernel.org"},{"name":"Paolo Abeni","address":"pabeni@redhat.com"},{"name":"Simon Horman","address":"horms@kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"dev@openvswitch.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"stable@vger.kernel.org"}],"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-16T14:52:33.000Z","iso":"2026-08-16T14:52:33.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"Re: [PATCH net] net: openvswitch: fix flow mask use-after-free on flow deletion","mailingLists":[{"id":"linux-kernel.vger.kernel.org","displayName":"linux-kernel.vger.kernel.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Ilya Maximets <i.maximets@ovn.org> writes:"},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"The commit in the Fixes tag below made so flow->mask free is scheduled"},{"depth":1,"text":"via RCU right after it is removed from the flow table.  The pointer"},{"depth":1,"text":"stays in the flow structure and it can be accessible while in the same"},{"depth":1,"text":"RCU critical section.  This is done to avoid requiring ovs_mutex for"},{"depth":1,"text":"the ovs_flow_free()."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"However, while removing the flow during processing of CMD_DEL, we do"},{"depth":1,"text":"not take RCU read lock before the removal, and ovs_flow_cmd_fill_info()"},{"depth":1,"text":"uses the flow->mask pointer afterwards.  The RCU read lock is taken,"},{"depth":1,"text":"but it's already late at that point.  The comment on that line"},{"depth":1,"text":"acknowledges that the lock is cosmetic and doesn't serve a real purpose."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"This leads to use-after-free if the RCU grace period passes between"},{"depth":1,"text":"removal and the filling.  It is a short race window, but it is there"},{"depth":1,"text":"and can lead to a real crash in case memory allocation for the info"},{"depth":1,"text":"takes a bit longer:"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":" BUG: KASAN: slab-use-after-free in __ovs_nla_put_key"},{"depth":1,"text":"             net/openvswitch/flow_netlink.c:1996"},{"depth":1,"text":" BUG: KASAN: slab-use-after-free in ovs_nla_put_key+0x2463/0x2e30"},{"depth":1,"text":"             net/openvswitch/flow_netlink.c:2250"},{"depth":1,"text":" Read of size 4 at addr ffff88801ee89970 by task ovs_flow_del_ec/9487"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":" Call Trace:"},{"depth":1,"text":"  <TASK>"},{"depth":1,"text":"  __ovs_nla_put_key net/openvswitch/flow_netlink.c:1996"},{"depth":1,"text":"  ovs_nla_put_key+0x2463/0x2e30 net/openvswitch/flow_netlink.c:2250"},{"depth":1,"text":"  ovs_flow_cmd_fill_info+0x420/0x9c0 net/openvswitch/datapath.c:930"},{"depth":1,"text":"  ovs_flow_cmd_del+0x53a/0x970 net/openvswitch/datapath.c:1467"},{"depth":1,"text":"  ..."},{"depth":1,"text":"  netlink_rcv_skb+0x156/0x420 net/netlink/af_netlink.c:2556"},{"depth":1,"text":"  </TASK>"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":" Allocated by task 9487:"},{"depth":1,"text":"  mask_alloc net/openvswitch/flow_table.c:967"},{"depth":1,"text":"  flow_mask_insert net/openvswitch/flow_table.c:1012"},{"depth":1,"text":"  ovs_flow_tbl_insert+0xea2/0x1a90 net/openvswitch/flow_table.c:1084"},{"depth":1,"text":"  ovs_flow_cmd_new+0x7e3/0xd90 net/openvswitch/datapath.c:1086"},{"depth":1,"text":"  ..."},{"depth":1,"text":"  netlink_rcv_skb+0x156/0x420 net/netlink/af_netlink.c:2556"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":" Freed by task 9485:"},{"depth":1,"text":"  rcu_free_sheaf+0x1e/0x100 mm/slub.c:5978"},{"depth":1,"text":"  rcu_do_batch kernel/rcu/tree.c:2645"},{"depth":1,"text":"  rcu_core+0x59c/0x10c0 kernel/rcu/tree.c:2897"},{"depth":1,"text":"  handle_softirqs+0x1e4/0x9a0 kernel/softirq.c:622"},{"depth":1,"text":"  ..."},{"depth":1,"text":"  instr_sysvec_apic_timer_interrupt arch/x86/kernel/apic/apic.c:1062"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"ovs_flow_tbl_remove() must be called after the ovs_flow_cmd_fill_info()"},{"depth":1,"text":"to avoid this race.  This also helps with cleaning up the forced cast"},{"depth":1,"text":"and the cosmetic RCU read lock.  Before the commit in the Fixes tag the"},{"depth":1,"text":"order did not matter as long as the flow object itself was not freed."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"A wider RCU critical section could be another option, but we have a"},{"depth":1,"text":"GFP_KERNEL allocation in the way."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Reported by Trend Micro's Zero Day Initiative as ZDI-CAN-32042."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Fixes: 56c19868e115 (\"openvswitch: Make flow mask removal symmetric.\")"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org"},{"depth":1,"text":"Signed-off-by: Ilya Maximets <i.maximets@ovn.org>"},{"depth":1,"text":"---"}],"lineCount":63,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Reviewed-by: Aaron Conole <aconole@redhat.com>"}],"patchIds":[],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":0,"diagnostics":[]}},"rootIds":["f7t5x1anmmm.fsf@aconole-thinkpadt14gen4.rmtusnh.csb"],"childrenByParent":{},"chronologicalIds":["f7t5x1anmmm.fsf@aconole-thinkpadt14gen4.rmtusnh.csb"],"patchSeries":[],"diagnostics":[],"patches":{}}}